-- title:
--   Commutativity of T_ℓ and T_{ℓ'} on J₀(N)(ℚ̄)
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $N, \ell, \ell', M$ with $N \neq 0$, $M \neq 0$, with $\ell$ and $\ell'$ prime, and two factorisation hypotheses $M = N\ell\ell'$ and $M = N\ell'\ell$. Assume that each of the base-changed modular function fields `modularFunctionFieldBar` of levels $N\ell$, $N\ell'$ and $M$ — the subextension of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the full modular function field of that level — satisfies `HasPrincipalDivisors` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$: every nonzero element $f$ admits a divisor $D$ with $D(v) = \operatorname{ord}_v f$ at every place $v$ and $\deg D = 0$. Assume further the two exchange hypotheses `HeckeExchangeAt` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, for $(N,\ell,\ell',M)$ and for $(N,\ell',\ell,M)$: granted integrality of the relevant degeneracy legs, for every divisor $D$ on the level-$N\ell'$ (respectively level-$N\ell$) field, the pullback along the substitution map `heckeBetaBar` of the pushforward along the inclusion `heckeAlphaBar` of $D$ coincides with the pushforward along the tower inclusion `towerInclBar` of the pullback along `towerSubstBar` of $D$. The conclusion is that the two endomorphisms `heckeOperatorBar N ⟨ℓ, _⟩` and `heckeOperatorBar N ⟨ℓ', _⟩` of the degree-zero divisor class group $J_0(N)$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, viewed in $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{Z}}$, commute.
--
--   This is the commutativity of the Hecke operators $T_\ell$ and $T_{\ell'}$ at distinct (or equal) primes acting on the Jacobian $J_0(N)$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, obtained here from the geometric exchange identity between the two modular correspondences over the roof level $N\ell\ell'$. It is the input to [`ModularCurve.heckeOperatorsCommuteBar_of_heckeExchangeAt`](thm.html#ModularCurve.heckeOperatorsCommuteBar_of_heckeExchangeAt), and hence to the commutative Hecke algebra structure used later.
